<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18851" root="ست" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاتٌّ</span></b>  [<i>Sixth</i>]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ فُلَانٌ سَادِسًا</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَادِيًا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاتًّا</span> [<i>Such a one came sixth</i>]; <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سادسا</span>
being formed from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِدْسٌ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ساتّا</span>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِتَّةٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِتٌّ</span>: in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ساديا</span>, the [latter] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">س</span> [of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سادسا</span>] is changed
into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span>; for certain letters in other cases are
sometimes so changed; as in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمَّا</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَا</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَنَّنَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَنَّى</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَضَّضَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَضَّى</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلَعَّعَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلَعَّى</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَرَّرَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسَرَّى</span>. (ISk, S.)

